Package: mortensor
Title: Flexible Mortality Forecasting Across Data Granularities
Version: 0.1.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Karl", "Emmert-Fees", email = "karl.emmert-fees@tum.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Tools to combine mortality and population data observed at
    different granularities (age groups, open age intervals, periods,
    population strata and causes) and to build probabilistic mortality
    forecasts from interchangeable parts: harmonisation and ungrouping with the
    penalized composite link model, Lee-Carter, random walk with drift and
    tensor (Tucker3) models, Bayesian age-period-cohort models through the
    'bamp' package, ensembles, honest rolling-origin backtests with proper
    scoring rules, and life tables computed from simulated paths.
